    "result_text": "The build succeeds and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `checkDigit` as a Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the owner's `customerCode`, following the existing conventions for read-only derived fields (like `membershipLevel`).\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Transient getCheckDigit()` getter that computes the Luhn check digit over the digits in `customerCode` (ignoring the `-` separators and letters), returning `null` when no `customerCode` has been assigned. The algorithm mirrors the standard Luhn computation the test harness uses.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `checkDigit` property (integer 0\u20139, `readOnly`) to the `Owner` schema. The build regenerates `OwnerDto` with this field, and MapStruct auto-maps it from `Owner.getCheckDigit()` \u2014 no explicit mapper entry needed, same as other getter-backed fields (`customerCode`, `membershipLevel`, etc.).\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` test passes, confirming the returned `checkDigit` exactly matches the Luhn digit recomputed from the returned `customerCode`, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
