    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe new `getCheckDigit()` lands exactly where a maintainer of this file would expect it. The Owner model already hosts a cluster of `@Transient`, read-only *derived* getters \u2014 `getMembershipLevel()` and `getIdentityKey()` \u2014 each a self-contained computation over the entity's own fields, documented with a Javadoc describing the derivation. `getCheckDigit()` matches that established pattern precisely: same `@Transient` annotation, same null-guard-then-compute shape, same documentation style, and it's placed directly between its two siblings rather than scattered elsewhere.\n\n- Logic is in the right unit: it derives purely from `customerCode`, a field of this entity, so computing it on the entity (not a service) is consistent with how `membershipLevel`/`identityKey` are already handled here.\n- Nothing is duplicated \u2014 the Luhn loop isn't repeated elsewhere, and there's no existing check-digit utility this would be reinventing.\n- The class isn't becoming a catch-all; this is one more cohesive derived property among several of the same kind.\n- The OpenAPI addition mirrors the adjacent `membershipLevel`/`bulkSignupWarning` read-only schema entries (title/description/type/`readOnly: true`, with sensible min/max 0\u20139), so the contract change is equally idiomatic.\n\nNo structural changes needed.",
